Patch summary:
Support Ika's interface modes. persist.sys.ika.mode ("tv" or "desktop"), which
IkaMode's switcher sets, takes effect at boot. SystemConfig also reads
etc/sysconfig/ika_<mode> and etc/permissions/ika_<mode> on /system_ext, which
hold TV mode's features, so that they exist only in a TV boot. PackageManager
scans the Android TV SystemUI, package installer and framework stubs only in
TV mode, and the desktop SystemUI and package installer only in desktop mode
(PackageInstaller_tv no longer overrides PackageInstaller at build time), and
keeps a separate package parser cache in TV mode: overlays gated on the mode
with requiredSystemPropertyName are skipped while parsing, but a cached parse
from the other mode would install them anyway. In TV mode the freeform
developer setting, which Cuttlefish's set_adb.sh keeps on for the desktop, no
longer turns freeform windowing back on.

Where the image also has the Android TV build of the Play Store (Tubesky,
which images with MindTheGapps carry next to the phone build, Phonesky),
PackageManager scans Tubesky only in TV mode and Phonesky only in desktop
mode, as the phone Play Store refuses to run on a TV. Images without Tubesky
keep the phone Play Store in both modes.

